{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options","id":1308634,"title":"Ignoring Aura Options.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-29T04:16:05-07:00","id":1308634,"title":"Ignoring Aura Options.","content":"OK so after a discussion with my players it appears Aura is a deal breaker. So anyone got any ideas of houserules to get past this?. What breaks if I just ignore this?.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/917-ancient-of-days","name":"Ancient of days","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T04:25:09-07:00","id":1308637,"title":"","content":"Aura unfortunately is a linchpin mechanic. I believe there are a few homebrews that don't have it. A clutch of dragons was one. Personally, i don't think much breaks with full access but I would treat off element moves with a slight xp surcharge to balance things out a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-29-2019, 07:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T04:59:02-07:00","id":1308641,"title":"","content":"It's always on but you can't combo two things that need different ones, maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T05:00:38-07:00","id":1308642,"title":"","content":"What was the main problem they had with it? That will help figure out what bits to keep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T05:38:02-07:00","id":1308652,"title":"","content":"If its problematic just treat yourself as having a 24/7 omni-aura. It makes DB's way stronger but I don't think it breaks anything.<br /> <br /> MA's may require a tiny bit more tweaking tho.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T06:11:44-07:00","id":1308659,"title":"","content":"It breaks a few Lore charms that mess with aura, like the one that gives your aura to someone else, and depending on how you run it it can make them pretty drastically more powerful, but not so much that they\u2019ll be more broken than Solars.<br /> <br /> Like for example if charms that say \u201cyou may expend your aura to blah blah blah\u201d and they always have that effect, and then you combo that charm with a signature charm of another element, it\u2019s a power boost to be sure. Especially at Essence 5 when you can start combining multiple different aspected signature charms. If you can handle Solar power though you can handle that easy.<br /> <br /> Oh yeah and comboing IMAs becomes very attractive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T06:13:22-07:00","id":1308660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1308659#post1308659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It breaks a few Lore charms that mess with aura, like the one that gives your aura to someone else, and depending on how you run it it can make them pretty drastically more powerful, but not so much that they\u2019ll be more broken than Solars.<br /> <br /> Like for example if charms that say \u201cyou may expend your aura to blah blah blah\u201d and they always have that effect, and then you combo that charm with a signature charm of another element, it\u2019s a power boost to be sure. Especially at Essence 5 when you can start combining multiple different aspected signature charms. If you can handle Solar power though you can handle that easy.<br /> <br /> Oh yeah and comboing IMAs becomes very attractive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would put aura effects as repurchases or anima effects that take 2-3 anima. The problem is some auras are the only thing making a charm useful. So you'd have to look at every power and then determine what would need restrictions and what wouldn't. <br /> <br /> Also, combing IMA should be attractive. Being a dragon blooded who mastered all five dragon styles should be fearsome not a joke.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-29-2019, 09:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T06:46:12-07:00","id":1308668,"title":"","content":"All five dragon styles feels like making a 5 colour deck in magic. It's potentially powerful, but you need to know what you're doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T06:47:45-07:00","id":1308669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1308668#post1308668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All five dragon styles feels like making a 5 colour deck in magic. It's potentially powerful, but you need to know what you're doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you read the styles as written? It'd be like a five colored deck that knee caps itself because it went five colors instead of mono. They don't work together at all in this edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T06:54:38-07:00","id":1308671,"title":"","content":"....When is it advisable to mix decks that much in magic? Your not supposed to try to mix them that much. To make it work you have to be an oddity, Like Myrrun. Myrrun isn't normal and that what makes him scary. Outside of him I haven't heard of any IM that try to mix the styles","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":3742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","user":"Iceblade44","date":". 04-29-2019, 09:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T07:15:23-07:00","id":1308676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1308671#post1308671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">....When is it advisable to mix decks that much in magic? Your not supposed to try to mix them that much. To make it work you have to be an oddity, Like Myrrun. Myrrun isn't normal and that what makes him scary. Outside of him I haven't heard of any IM that try to mix the styles</div> </div> </div> </div>Five color decks can be unstoppable if you have the right cards. Due to how the best land cards are insanely expensive. it's just throwing money at your table to make it work. Also, two to three color decks are the norm depending on the lands you can acquire. I mean it's kind of a poor analogy.<br /> <br /> In previous editions, you'd have dragon blooded with multiple styles outside of Myrrun but now any dragon blooded who tries it just screws himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T07:15:56-07:00","id":1308677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1308660#post1308660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would put aura effects as repurchases or anima effects that take 2-3 anima. The problem is some auras are the only thing making a charm useful. So you'd have to look at every power and then determine what would need restrictions and what wouldn't. <br /> <br /> Also, combing IMA should be attractive. Being a dragon blooded who mastered all five dragon styles should be fearsome not a joke.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s true, also it won\u2019t even be as overpowered as comboing an IMA with half of the overpowered corebook styles. Fire Dragon with Steel Devil, Snake and Air Dragon, ect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T07:18:53-07:00","id":1308678,"title":"","content":"That first example is kind of a not a good example because fire dragon sucks and so does steel devil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T07:46:32-07:00","id":1308682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1308678#post1308678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That first example is kind of a not a good example because fire dragon sucks and so does steel devil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Steel Devil sucks against very high skill opponents, and is complete garbage agains anyone with a good onslaught penalty negator, but Fire Dragon is okay, and the two of them together are completely bonkerz.<br /> <br /> First turn spend 15m to activate Naked Fang Draw and Flash Fire Technique. Beat everyone in initiative and reflexively fill up your offhand charge, as well as enter Comsuming Might of the Fire Dragon, to ensure that you go first even if you dumped a bunch of initiative into your charge. Then attack and even against foes with 5 Defense you only need 9 successes to Triple Attack Technique them, and even with the terrestrial keyword it\u2019ll make your attack deal +17 withering damage plus any remaining overflow successes, and then activate Steel Devil Strike, which gets (Dexterity) overflow successes to damage because of Flash Fire Technique, one die for Consuming Might of the Fire Dragon, and a full excellency of successes on the attack roll, not that it really matters because their Defense is at -4 due to onslaught, and now every one of your allies has that benefit as well.<br /> <br /> If you\u2019re facing a Dawn with a medium weapon and Hail Shattering Practice, it\u2019s trash, if you\u2019re facing a stone skinned earth elemental with 20 soak, 30 health levels and 12 Hardness, it\u2019s great.<br /> <br /> EDIT: actually forget what I said, it\u2019s still good against a lot of high skill opponents, just as long as they don\u2019t have a good onslaught penalty negator. I forgot about the trick of delaying your action until after the enemy, attacking them to knock their initiative down below yours, then attacking them again right after once the round resets. With that strategy even if they have a Defense of 7 all you need to do is hit 11 successes on the first attack to get a double and then triple attack off. That\u2019s also assuming you\u2019re alone too, which most PCs should almost never be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 04-29-2019, 12:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T09:36:10-07:00","id":1308700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1308682#post1308682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Steel Devil sucks against very high skill opponents, and is complete garbage agains anyone with a good onslaught penalty negator, but Fire Dragon is okay, and the two of them together are completely bonkerz.<br /> <br /> First turn spend 15m to activate Naked Fang Draw and Flash Fire Technique. Beat everyone in initiative and reflexively fill up your offhand charge, as well as enter Comsuming Might of the Fire Dragon, to ensure that you go first even if you dumped a bunch of initiative into your charge. Then attack and even against foes with 5 Defense you only need 9 successes to Triple Attack Technique them, and even with the terrestrial keyword it\u2019ll make your attack deal +17 withering damage plus any remaining overflow successes, and then activate Steel Devil Strike, which gets (Dexterity) overflow successes to damage because of Flash Fire Technique, one die for Consuming Might of the Fire Dragon, and a full excellency of successes on the attack roll, not that it really matters because their Defense is at -4 due to onslaught, and now every one of your allies has that benefit as well.<br /> <br /> If you\u2019re facing a Dawn with a medium weapon and Hail Shattering Practice, it\u2019s trash, if you\u2019re facing a stone skinned earth elemental with 20 soak, 30 health levels and 12 Hardness, it\u2019s great.<br /> <br /> EDIT: actually forget what I said, it\u2019s still good against a lot of high skill opponents, just as long as they don\u2019t have a good onslaught penalty negator. I forgot about the trick of delaying your action until after the enemy, attacking them to knock their initiative down below yours, then attacking them again right after once the round resets. With that strategy even if they have a Defense of 7 all you need to do is hit 11 successes on the first attack to get a double and then triple attack off. That\u2019s also assuming you\u2019re alone too, which most PCs should almost never be.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would try to stop assuming everyone is Essence 5 in test scenarios. Consuming Might of the Fire Dragon is not a balance point for how bad the style is in general, which is mostly a symptom of it being an alpha strike style. And most games stop by E3, let alone 4 or 5, so you never get to use those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T09:39:52-07:00","id":1308701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ancient of days</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options#post1308634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK so after a discussion with my players it appears Aura is a deal breaker. So anyone got any ideas of houserules to get past this?. What breaks if I just ignore this?.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You can do several things to make it easier on your players:<br /> <br /> 1) Ignore Aura-lock at Bonfire, and/or allow Reflexive out-of-turn Charms to create Aura as much as they can disrupt it. This makes several things MUCH more attractive without completely breaking the intended balance for DBs.<br /> <br /> 2) As Sandact said, make it so that the PC DBs are ALWAYS treated as being in all five auras, all the time, which kind of breaks them balance-wise but also makes their kit feel so much better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T10:02:23-07:00","id":1308711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1308701#post1308701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> 2) As Sandact said, make it so that the PC DBs are ALWAYS treated as being in all five auras, all the time, which kind of breaks them balance-wise but also makes their kit feel so much better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even with aura effects their charms are pretty much a tier lower than either solars or lunars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T10:17:45-07:00","id":1308715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1308700#post1308700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would try to stop assuming everyone is Essence 5 in test scenarios. Consuming Might of the Fire Dragon is not a balance point for how bad the style is in general, which is mostly a symptom of it being an alpha strike style. And most games stop by E3, let alone 4 or 5, so you never get to use those.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, but everything still works at Essence 2, and for a DB at Essence 3 it already caps your autosuccesses. <br /> <br /> If we\u2019re talking E3 and you\u2019re trying to stop, I dunno something tough as nails like a herd of stampeding Pestletails sent to raze a village to the ground by an angry god, it\u2019s good. With exactly average rolls you almost kill one of the pestletails right out of the gate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T11:15:24-07:00","id":1308725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1308715#post1308715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair enough, but everything still works at Essence 2, and for a DB at Essence 3 it already caps your autosuccesses.<br /> <br /> If we\u2019re talking E3 and you\u2019re trying to stop, I dunno something tough as nails like a herd of stampeding Pestletails sent to raze a village to the ground by an angry god, it\u2019s good. With exactly average rolls you almost kill one of the pestletails right out of the gate.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And then stay moteless for about 5 rounds. See, the E2 strategy with Fire Dragon (Which is the same strategy up until E5, when you can FINALLY breathe a little) is to:<br /> <br /> 1) Get the best Join Battle possible by throwing 17 motes at Flash Fire Technique + Awareness Excellency<br /> <br /> 2) Reflexively activate the Form Charm<br /> <br /> 3) Use the Fire Aspect anima power of once per day +(Intimacy) non-Charm dice to supplement a decisive attack, then throw Perfect Blazing Blow at it for a max of +2 or +3 non-Charm successes on the attack roll, thus ending up with a max of +4 dice +3 sux all Non-Charm to ensure a huge attack roll, besides of course a full excellency. Since the Form Charm applies onslaught before your attack happens, it's effectively another +1 non-Charm success unless they have onslaught negators.<br /> <br /> 4) Flash-Fire Technique converts threshold successes on the attack roll to the damage roll as dice, which get reroll 6s due to the excellency, up to +5 damage. Assuming you got, let's say, 13 initiative because you rolled 10 successes on 17 dice in Join Battle (you got lucky in one of your two rolls in Flash Fire), this makes it 18 dice of damage, and all 6s create more dice of damage as well. If your Lore-specced friend reflexively passed Fire Aura onto you, or you had it before the fight began, you also add up to +2 or +3 damage dice from Perfect Blazing Blow. Let's say this all amounts to 23 dice of damage (two or three sixes rerolled), when you started with a mere 13.<br /> <br /> 5) You instakilled one opponent straight out of Join Battle, congratulations! Now do basically nothing for the next five rounds as you recover the 27 motes, 1wp you just paid to enable the entire thing, and can't do as good until an entire day passes. But hey at least your anima flux is doing something! Maybe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T11:16:43-07:00","id":1308726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1308711#post1308711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even with aura effects their charms are pretty much a tier lower than either solars or lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not always! DBs ignore wound penalties better than Lunars do with Unflagging Vengeance Meditation, ignoring a full -4 wound penalty while Relentless Lunar Fury only halves those. Other examples exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T11:19:10-07:00","id":1308732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1308726#post1308726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not always! DBs ignore wound penalties better than Lunars do with Unflagging Vengeance Meditation, ignoring a full -4 wound penalty while Relentless Lunar Fury only halves those. Other examples exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>That a charm that works in a very narrow context and doesn't remotely have the applicability that Relentless lunar fury does. If I remember correctly, lunars also have better basic ways to negate penalties than dragon blooded do.<br /> <br /> Edit- I think you mean Wound-Denying Dragon Faith and it only applies when you have an intimacy. Granted Unflagging vengeance Meditation gives you an appropriate one but by that point lunars have a version of relentless lunar fury which is about 20x better due to how much that upgrade tree boosts the performance of that tree.<br /> <br /> There really is no point when a dragon blooded and celestial at equal xp are going to be on any even footing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-29-2019, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T11:21:52-07:00","id":1308733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1308732#post1308732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That a charm that works in a very narrow context and doesn't remotely have the applicability that Relentless lunar fury does. If I remember correctly, lunars also have better basic ways to negate penalties than dragon blooded do.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Applicability being &quot;Risk dying from a decisive attack&quot;, instead of &quot;Activate at will when upholding an Intimacy&quot;, gotcha. Unflagging is even cheaper than RLF. Regardless, yes, most of their Charms are still inferior but omni-Aura breaks them due to combinatorial hell, not due to individually potent magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T11:29:55-07:00","id":1308739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1308733#post1308733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Applicability being &quot;Risk dying from a decisive attack&quot;, instead of &quot;Activate at will when upholding an Intimacy&quot;, gotcha. Unflagging is even cheaper than RLF. Regardless, yes, most of their Charms are still inferior but omni-Aura breaks them due to combinatorial hell, not due to individually potent magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? What exactly is a problem here? Even combined a dragon blooded doesn't have charms comparable to other exalts. Like look at their defenses most of these are lacking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T11:54:24-07:00","id":1308749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1308739#post1308739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? What exactly is a problem here? Even combined a dragon blooded doesn't have charms comparable to other exalts. Like look at their defenses most of these are lacking.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Combine Eye of the Wood Dragon, Perfect Blazing Blow and Force of the Mountain, all with Aura effects. Combine Flame-Borne Interception and Aura-Graceful Flowing Defense to both ignore 3 onslaught penalties AND raise your Parry for a whole round at 6m, 1i (Also known as &quot;already worth the cost by the first time it matters, let alone if getting ganged up on). Use Burning Pinnacle Strike without need to be careful about sustaining Aura, allowing you to combine it with things like Demon-Crushing Wolf Bite. Comboing all Wood, Earth and Water Aura Brawl Charms related to clinches. This is all Essence 1-2 by the way, it gets even more silly with Signatures which often require Aura. That said, I DO prefer DBs to feel stronger than they do now, at least PC ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T12:20:00-07:00","id":1308755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1308749#post1308749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Combine Eye of the Wood Dragon, Perfect Blazing Blow and Force of the Mountain, all with Aura effects. Combine Flame-Borne Interception and Aura-Graceful Flowing Defense to both ignore 3 onslaught penalties AND raise your Parry for a whole round at 6m, 1i (Also known as &quot;already worth the cost by the first time it matters, let alone if getting ganged up on). Use Burning Pinnacle Strike without need to be careful about sustaining Aura, allowing you to combine it with things like Demon-Crushing Wolf Bite. Comboing all Wood, Earth and Water Aura Brawl Charms related to clinches. This is all Essence 1-2 by the way, it gets even more silly with Signatures which often require Aura. That said, I DO prefer DBs to feel stronger than they do now, at least PC ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds nice but none of it is remotely as powerful as what either lunars or solars get. They get stronger charms that combine better and apply more. A solar dodger can ignore all penalties and raise evasion with just 1m and 1i per evasion and increase their cap by essence. Solar brawl hell just heaven solar hammer is stronger than anything brawl can combine. That's one charm better than the entire dragon blooded brawl charmset and it's at start. I have not seen a single effect with aura that even matches up to what solars or even lunars get outside a minor example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-29-2019, 04:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T12:31:54-07:00","id":1308758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1308725#post1308725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And then stay moteless for about 5 rounds. See, the E2 strategy with Fire Dragon (Which is the same strategy up until E5, when you can FINALLY breathe a little) is to:<br /> <br /> 1) Get the best Join Battle possible by throwing 17 motes at Flash Fire Technique + Awareness Excellency<br /> <br /> 2) Reflexively activate the Form Charm<br /> <br /> 3) Use the Fire Aspect anima power of once per day +(Intimacy) non-Charm dice to supplement a decisive attack, then throw Perfect Blazing Blow at it for a max of +2 or +3 non-Charm successes on the attack roll, thus ending up with a max of +4 dice +3 sux all Non-Charm to ensure a huge attack roll, besides of course a full excellency. Since the Form Charm applies onslaught before your attack happens, it's effectively another +1 non-Charm success unless they have onslaught negators.<br /> <br /> 4) Flash-Fire Technique converts threshold successes on the attack roll to the damage roll as dice, which get reroll 6s due to the excellency, up to +5 damage. Assuming you got, let's say, 13 initiative because you rolled 10 successes on 17 dice in Join Battle (you got lucky in one of your two rolls in Flash Fire), this makes it 18 dice of damage, and all 6s create more dice of damage as well. If your Lore-specced friend reflexively passed Fire Aura onto you, or you had it before the fight began, you also add up to +2 or +3 damage dice from Perfect Blazing Blow. Let's say this all amounts to 23 dice of damage (two or three sixes rerolled), when you started with a mere 13.<br /> <br /> 5) You instakilled one opponent straight out of Join Battle, congratulations! Now do basically nothing for the next five rounds as you recover the 27 motes, 1wp you just paid to enable the entire thing, and can't do as good until an entire day passes. But hey at least your anima flux is doing something! Maybe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay so let\u2019s do the same thing with a combined Steel Devil Stylist, I\u2019ll even be very generous to your Fire Dragon purist and not have an applicable specialty, or use anima powers, or have a friend who\u2019s species into lore here. Although I appreciate the teamwork.<br /> <br /> <br /> Start out 15m Naked Fang Draw and Flash Fire, were JB with +2 successes.<br /> <br /> So we\u2019re rolling 12 dice since we don\u2019t have an applicable specialty but we can stunt it and it\u2019s not an opposed roll so we can\u2019t just say the effect is canceled by a stunt on the other side. Plus stunting JB is easy with a character this cool. Let\u2019s even say we roll bad and even with two chances we can\u2019t roll better than average so we get 6 becoming 11 initiative.<br /> <br /> Now we won JB so we get a free charge from Naked Fang Draw, we can reflexively enter Fire Dragon, and dump another 9 init into charge to max it out.<br /> <br /> Now if we\u2019re attacking somebody who has 4 parry, we only need 6 successes for triple attack technique, and it doesn\u2019t even matter if it\u2019s 4 parry because their base is 4, or because it\u2019s 5 and somebody already laid an onslaught penalty on them or what. It could even have been 7 and somebody knocked them to the ground with a smash attack or something. After dumping so much init into our charge it\u2019s likely one of our hearth mates went before us anyway. With a single excellency die on that we\u2019re getting 17 so let\u2019s say we roll under average yet again and get only 7.<br /> <br /> So we hit with triple attack and one success over for a total damage bonus, with 5 strength, of +28, and lets say that along with their good parry they had a solid soak of 12 as well, so we\u2019re dealing 16 withering damage. <br /> <br /> Rolling that damage and rerolling 6s lets say we get 9, which crashes our target. So we have 15 initiative from that and can pay 5m 1wp to Steel Devil Strike. We won\u2019t need to excellency this more than 1m either, our target has a -4 onslaught penalty on it already. We hit with 5 overflow easy and deal 20 decisive damage, just under what your fire aspect rolled and for 20m 1wp, since we regenerated 5m at the start of the turn. <br /> <br /> Doesn\u2019t seem much better eh? But here\u2019s the differences:<br /> <br /> It doesn\u2019t work against anyone with a good onslaught penalty negator, which I feel like people reading this will forget I said, even though I\u2019ve put this here.<br /> <br /> We crashed the crap out of one enemy<br /> <br /> We added a -4 onslaught penalty to that same enemy<br /> <br /> We didn\u2019t use our anima power or need an ally species in anything but \u201chas an attack\u201d<br /> <br /> We\u2019re sitting with a Steel Devil offhand charge of 10, which means the only difference between the attack combo we launched this turn and the one we\u2019re going to launch next turn is that we won\u2019t be getting that 5 overflow from Flash Fire. It if we want to conserve motes and willpower just launch a triple attack technique and crash another enemy into the ground with a big onslaught penalty and just keep the initiative for 3m.<br /> <br /> <br /> Is it better in all situations? Hell no! But it\u2019s definitely not crap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T13:07:58-07:00","id":1308767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1308758#post1308758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay so let\u2019s do the same thing with a combined Steel Devil Stylist, I\u2019ll even be very generous to your Fire Dragon purist and not have an applicable specialty, or use anima powers, or have a friend who\u2019s species into lore here. Although I appreciate the teamwork.<br /> <br /> <br /> Start out 15m Naked Fang Draw and Flash Fire, were JB with +2 successes.<br /> <br /> So we\u2019re rolling 12 dice since we don\u2019t have an applicable specialty but we can stunt it and it\u2019s not an opposed roll so we can\u2019t just say the effect is canceled by a stunt on the other side. Plus stunting JB is easy with a character this cool. Let\u2019s even say we roll bad and even with two chances we can\u2019t roll better than average so we get 6 becoming 11 initiative.<br /> <br /> Now we won JB so we get a free charge from Naked Fang Draw, we can reflexively enter Fire Dragon, and dump another 9 init into charge to max it out.<br /> <br /> Now if we\u2019re attacking somebody who has 4 parry, we only need 6 successes for triple attack technique, and it doesn\u2019t even matter if it\u2019s 4 parry because their base is 4, or because it\u2019s 5 and somebody already laid an onslaught penalty on them or what. It could even have been 7 and somebody knocked them to the ground with a smash attack or something. After dumping so much init into our charge it\u2019s likely one of our hearth mates went before us anyway. With a single excellency die on that we\u2019re getting 17 so let\u2019s say we roll under average yet again and get only 7.<br /> <br /> So we hit with triple attack and one success over for a total damage bonus, with 5 strength, of +28, and lets say that along with their good parry they had a solid soak of 12 as well, so we\u2019re dealing 16 withering damage.<br /> <br /> Rolling that damage and rerolling 6s lets say we get 9, which crashes our target. So we have 15 initiative from that and can pay 5m 1wp to Steel Devil Strike. We won\u2019t need to excellency this more than 1m either, our target has a -4 onslaught penalty on it already. We hit with 5 overflow easy and deal 20 decisive damage, just under what your fire aspect rolled and for 20m 1wp, since we regenerated 5m at the start of the turn.<br /> <br /> Doesn\u2019t seem much better eh? But here\u2019s the differences:<br /> <br /> It doesn\u2019t work against anyone with a good onslaught penalty negator, which I feel like people reading this will forget I said, even though I\u2019ve put this here.<br /> <br /> We crashed the crap out of one enemy<br /> <br /> We added a -4 onslaught penalty to that same enemy<br /> <br /> We didn\u2019t use our anima power or need an ally species in anything but \u201chas an attack\u201d<br /> <br /> We\u2019re sitting with a Steel Devil offhand charge of 10, which means the only difference between the attack combo we launched this turn and the one we\u2019re going to launch next turn is that we won\u2019t be getting that 5 overflow from Flash Fire. It if we want to conserve motes and willpower just launch a triple attack technique and crash another enemy into the ground with a big onslaught penalty and just keep the initiative for 3m.<br /> <br /> <br /> Is it better in all situations? Hell no! But it\u2019s definitely not crap.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not disagreeing with you regarding Steel Devil pairing (although I abhor how poorly written and balanced Steel Devil is), I'm saying that Fire Dragon's whole shtick is to go all out on the first round and absolutely obliterate someone and then spend several rounds doing nothing or attacking/defending without excellencies to go back to a decent number of motes, which I don't like. Alpha strike builds per se are dangerous to the game. You fight a single foe and insta-kill them? That's boring! You fight several ones and are now tapped out of motes after defeating a single one instantly, hence making you rely on your friends if any in order to recover some motes and do anything else at all? That feels bad!<br /> <br /> Let alone how much better styles like Earth and Water Dragon are in that they can simply allow you to hold your own for a combat of any length. Earth remains stable and powerful at any time, and Water feels like climbing uphill, with each wound penalty you take making them more and more dangerous. Fire feels like being amazing for three seconds and then useless the rest of the fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T16:34:22-07:00","id":1308822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1308767#post1308767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let alone how much better styles like Earth and Water Dragon are in that they can simply allow you to hold your own for a combat of any length. Earth remains stable and powerful at any time, and Water feels like climbing uphill, with each wound penalty you take making them more and more dangerous. Fire feels like being amazing for three seconds and then useless the rest of the fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of this applies to dragonblooded in bed too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T00:00:58-07:00","id":1308895,"title":"","content":"I think the idea with fire is that you're supposed to win in those three seconds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T01:05:58-07:00","id":1308898,"title":"","content":"Mechanics-wise a master of all five Dragon styles will always be a joke because they have well over 50 charms, most of which are redundant with eachother. Nixing Aura won\u2019t change that or how much essence it would take to use them in tandem, or how much more the styles synergize with themselves than eachother.<br /> <br /> You can make a custom charm or a QC that fulfills that role, though,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T06:28:24-07:00","id":1308916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1308898#post1308898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mechanics-wise a master of all five Dragon styles will always be a joke because they have well over 50 charms, most of which are redundant with eachother. Nixing Aura won\u2019t change that or how much essence it would take to use them in tandem, or how much more the styles synergize with themselves than eachother.<br /> <br /> You can make a custom charm or a QC that fulfills that role, though,</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Except nixing Aura and saying &quot;You always have omni-Aura, even in Bonfire&quot; effectively makes a master of all five Dragon Styles the scariest thing ever. Just comboing the workhorses freely is enough to be horrifying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T06:28:58-07:00","id":1308917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1308895#post1308895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the idea with fire is that you're supposed to win in those three seconds.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, if you're going against a single enemy. Not the case? You're fucked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T10:52:39-07:00","id":1308970,"title":"","content":"so to get back to the aura bypass idea, what if you just treat all charms <i>other than</i> aura keyword as being balanced? That and ignore aura-lock from bonfire anima. <br /> <br /> You'd only be able to use individual aura charms, thus avoiding overlapping the most powerful effects. You'd still need to set up for the most powerful stuff, but you could freely combo charms that are less powerful but normally off-limits because of elemental associations. <br /> <br /> You'd still end up with more powerful DB overall, but I think you'd still limit the use of the ultra-powerful stuff somewhat. Plus you'd get access to all the stuff you purchased as prerequisites to get to the higher end stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T10:55:16-07:00","id":1308972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1308970#post1308970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so to get back to the aura bypass idea, what if you just treat all charms <i>other than</i> aura keyword as being balanced? That and ignore aura-lock from bonfire anima.<br /> <br /> You'd only be able to use individual aura charms, thus avoiding overlapping the most powerful effects. You'd still need to set up for the most powerful stuff, but you could freely combo charms that are less powerful but normally off-limits because of elemental associations.<br /> <br /> You'd still end up with more powerful DB overall, but I think you'd still limit the use of the ultra-powerful stuff somewhat. Plus you'd get access to all the stuff you purchased as prerequisites to get to the higher end stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That sounds like a more balanced (heh) version of omni-aura, for sure. Could be a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T15:55:45-07:00","id":1309030,"title":"","content":"I don't know about Fire Dragon being useless. Yes, they get to spend a whole lot of essence in the beggining, and is outright deadly in the first turn. But it's hard even for a DB to be without any just like that - they have enough to use in the rest of combat. When the fire anima is at bonfire, their anima effect do 3i damage per turn on targets without hardness or crashed. Mixing it with Snake worked very well - both styles depend on being ahead of initiative, but have a wonderful synergy (+dex damage from snake with the DB Excellency re-rolls to damage).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T16:05:23-07:00","id":1309031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1309030#post1309030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know about Fire Dragon being useless. Yes, they get to spend a whole lot of essence in the beggining, and is outright deadly in the first turn. But it's hard even for a DB to be without any just like that - they have enough to use in the rest of combat. When the fire anima is at bonfire, their anima effect do 3i damage per turn on targets without hardness or crashed. Mixing it with Snake worked very well - both styles depend on being ahead of initiative, but have a wonderful synergy (+dex damage from snake with the DB Excellency re-rolls to damage).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The first round combo, assuming you're using no other styles, just Fire Dragon, costs 27m 1wp. Essence 2 Dragon-Blooded have 13 personal motes and 31 peripheral motes. This depletes 27 out of your 44m, more than half of them. If you even try to excellency defenses past this threshold, it's already going to mean being almost out of motes by your next turn. Your anima flux does not matter for the more important opponents unless your allies managed to crash someone, otherwise they will most of the time have ways around it like a Resistance Charm to get Hardness or just being a Dragon-Blooded. What are your options to climb back out of base initiative? The excellency. Searing Edge Attack does not aid you in gaining initiative whatsoever unless you crash someone, and with no other damage boosters that's looking kind of rough. It's not even THAT deadly at the beginning of combat unless they roll REALLY well on one of their two Join Battle rolls. They certainly don't have enough to use the rest of the combat - Searing Edge barely helps at all, Perfect Blazing Blow takes WP, and anything beyond either takes initiative, WP, or in general does not help them climb back up and do another decisive attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T16:12:45-07:00","id":1309032,"title":"","content":"Combining with other styles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T16:23:47-07:00","id":1309034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1309032#post1309032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Combining with other styles.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> -only helps contribute to the mote loss. Even then, I don't know of any styles that severely, severely push withering boosters in their 2-3 Charms pre-Form, and post-Form is too much investment by then considering you also have five Charms at least in Fire Dragon. At best, you could get away with grabbing two or three dots in different styles and only buying their withering enhancers, like Ebon Shadow and Snake. Or, stay happy spending all your Dragon XP on a single withering-heavy style and hoping the synergy is worth it. In general, I wish Fire Dragon had more applicability and was overall as strong in all situations as Earth and Water are. Those are powerful in basically every single encounter AND can alpha-strike you just as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T11:32:18-07:00","id":1309236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1309031#post1309031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first round combo, assuming you're using no other styles, just Fire Dragon, costs 27m 1wp. Essence 2 Dragon-Blooded have 13 personal motes and 31 peripheral motes. This depletes 27 out of your 44m, more than half of them. If you even try to excellency defenses past this threshold, it's already going to mean being almost out of motes by your next turn. Your anima flux does not matter for the more important opponents unless your allies managed to crash someone, otherwise they will most of the time have ways around it like a Resistance Charm to get Hardness or just being a Dragon-Blooded. What are your options to climb back out of base initiative? The excellency. Searing Edge Attack does not aid you in gaining initiative whatsoever unless you crash someone, and with no other damage boosters that's looking kind of rough. It's not even THAT deadly at the beginning of combat unless they roll REALLY well on one of their two Join Battle rolls. They certainly don't have enough to use the rest of the combat - Searing Edge barely helps at all, Perfect Blazing Blow takes WP, and anything beyond either takes initiative, WP, or in general does not help them climb back up and do another decisive attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me try to show what I did when I was taking tough enemies - I did not need to use all the charms all the time:<br /> <br /> Initiative Roll: Flash Fire Technique + Full Excellency (used just once, if the first roll was good, the second roll was a safety policy): 11 motes, 1wp (it was before the final edition, would be cheaper).<br /> Gained Initiative(usually)? -&gt; Fire Dragon Form: 7m<br /> Attack: Perfect Blazing Blow + Full Excellency: (9m, 1wp) - At this point, he had Dragon Graced Weapon (air), which gave the target -1 until the end of his next roll.<br /> <br /> Total Cost: 27m, 2wp - This would be 1wp cheaper now.<br /> <br /> The Initiative was usually on the about 15 or so. That was followed by an decisive attack for which that already had onslaught, and did 20L (with 2 double 9s - which each gave more damage die, and re-rolling all 6s). The target would be on the -2s if he was really tough, and the action would be raised to -3 by DGW. That opened the target to the other DBs, that capitalized on the target's low defense and/or forced him to bleed motes. <br /> <br /> He had melee as well, and had the options of using Stoking Bonfire Style flame-bourne interception and blinding spark distraction. On the next attacks, he had the option of using withering attacks with Stoking Bonfire Style, which would reduce in cost as is was being used. Then, as he gained initiative over the target, he could do fire dragon attacks. And if the target got crashed by him or other DB, he would take Anima damage (or bleed motes if he had a charm). <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T11:58:00-07:00","id":1309241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1309236#post1309236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let me try to show what I did when I was taking tough enemies - I did not need to use all the charms all the time:<br /> <br /> Initiative Roll: Flash Fire Technique + Full Excellency (used just once, if the first roll was good, the second roll was a safety policy): 11 motes, 1wp (it was before the final edition, would be cheaper).<br /> Gained Initiative(usually)? -&gt; Fire Dragon Form: 7m<br /> Attack: Perfect Blazing Blow + Full Excellency: (9m, 1wp) - At this point, he had Dragon Graced Weapon (air), which gave the target -1 until the end of his next roll.<br /> <br /> Total Cost: 27m, 2wp - This would be 1wp cheaper now.<br /> <br /> The Initiative was usually on the about 15 or so. That was followed by an decisive attack for which that already had onslaught, and did 20L (with 2 double 9s - which each gave more damage die, and re-rolling all 6s). The target would be on the -2s if he was really tough, and the action would be raised to -3 by DGW. That opened the target to the other DBs, that capitalized on the target's low defense and/or forced him to bleed motes.<br /> <br /> He had melee as well, and had the options of using Stoking Bonfire Style flame-bourne interception and blinding spark distraction. On the next attacks, he had the option of using withering attacks with Stoking Bonfire Style, which would reduce in cost as is was being used. Then, as he gained initiative over the target, he could do fire dragon attacks. And if the target got crashed by him or other DB, he would take Anima damage (or bleed motes if he had a charm).<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You just posted the exact same cost I said. 27m, 1wp. That said, the double 9s from Perfect Blazing Blow is on the attack roll, not the damage roll. And once again, you just said exactly what I did in the end. &quot;You open up with a great attack, and then your mates follow up and finish the cleanup while you're useless until you gain more initiative, which Fire Dragon does not help with at all&quot;. Having Melee too is not an excuse, Fire Dragon should work on its own without needing to buy up Charms in other Abilities, the same way Earth and Water do. Except other Martial Arts Styles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T12:46:02-07:00","id":1309260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1308767#post1308767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not disagreeing with you regarding Steel Devil pairing (although I abhor how poorly written and balanced Steel Devil is), I'm saying that Fire Dragon's whole shtick is to go all out on the first round and absolutely obliterate someone and then spend several rounds doing nothing or attacking/defending without excellencies to go back to a decent number of motes, which I don't like. Alpha strike builds per se are dangerous to the game. You fight a single foe and insta-kill them? That's boring! You fight several ones and are now tapped out of motes after defeating a single one instantly, hence making you rely on your friends if any in order to recover some motes and do anything else at all? That feels bad!<br /> <br /> Let alone how much better styles like Earth and Water Dragon are in that they can simply allow you to hold your own for a combat of any length. Earth remains stable and powerful at any time, and Water feels like climbing uphill, with each wound penalty you take making them more and more dangerous. Fire feels like being amazing for three seconds and then useless the rest of the fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Steel Devil is definitely not balanced well with the other core styles, and I've never found a way to make it work well against foes with onslaught penalty negators. It's not completely useless, but it's definitely harder hit than other styles when they come up against a type of enemy that they're bad at fighting. You could say it's balanced out by how amazing it is against the enemies that it's good at fighting, but I'm kind of eh on that logic. It's really just got one schtick<br /> <br /> <br /> Fire Dragon though, I totally disagree. The only charm that encourages you to do a turn 1 alpha strike is Flash Fire Technique. In fact Flame-Flicker Stance, Perfect Blazing Blow, Essence Igniting Nerve Strike, and Smoldering Wound Attack all encourage you not to do that. They're all either defensive charms with bonuses against lower initiative foes, something you're not likely to get after resetting to base initiative, withering attacks with bonuses against lower initiative foes, something that's not going to alpha strike, or decisive attacks with extra bonuses against crashed foes, something you're not going to get off turn 1.<br /> <br /> Flash-Fire Technique gives you the <i>option </i>to just kill somebody right off the bat if you want to, sure, that's your choice and maybe in some cases it's the right one. Like maybe the Raksha lord that you're having dinner with has just implied that he's going to splinter the mind of one of the other guests, and you want to kill him before he gets the chance to act. That'd be a good time to do it. After that you're spent and need to rely on your allies, but that's what allies are for, and if you weren't there to kill that Raksha in one chop who knows what could have happened.<br /> <br /> On the other hand if you're facing a pair of Blood Apes with your circle and don't really feel the need to blow out your entire mote pool and half your willpower killing one of them, then don't. Remember, the lesson of Hesiesh is knowing when and how to restrain yourself. In that case just forgo Flash Fire, or use it raw without enhancing both rolls if you just want consistency, and fight using Searing Edge Attacks and/or Essence Igniting Nerve Strikes if you think they're going to be crashed. With Fire Dragon Form up you can save 2m per attack and have about the same odds of hitting after all.<br /> <br /> Then if you want you can Perfect Blazing Blow, or Fiery Blade Attack them to finish them off, or even just regular decisive them. Or be a total dick and hit a spirit with a God-Immolating Strike and a Fiery Blade Attack and set them on double-fire. There's tons of options that aren't turn 1 decisive alpha strikes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T12:57:00-07:00","id":1309263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1309260#post1309260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, Steel Devil is definitely not balanced well with the other core styles, and I've never found a way to make it work well against foes with onslaught penalty negators. It's not completely useless, but it's definitely harder hit than other styles when they come up against a type of enemy that they're bad at fighting. You could say it's balanced out by how amazing it is against the enemies that it's good at fighting, but I'm kind of eh on that logic. It's really just got one schtick<br /> <br /> <br /> Fire Dragon though, I totally disagree. The only charm that encourages you to do a turn 1 alpha strike is Flash Fire Technique. In fact Flame-Flicker Stance, Perfect Blazing Blow, Essence Igniting Nerve Strike, and Smoldering Wound Attack all encourage you not to do that. They're all either defensive charms with bonuses against lower initiative foes, something you're not likely to get after resetting to base initiative, withering attacks with bonuses against lower initiative foes, something that's not going to alpha strike, or decisive attacks with extra bonuses against crashed foes, something you're not going to get off turn 1.<br /> <br /> Flash-Fire Technique gives you the <i>option </i>to just kill somebody right off the bat if you want to, sure, that's your choice and maybe in some cases it's the right one. Like maybe the Raksha lord that you're having dinner with has just implied that he's going to splinter the mind of one of the other guests, and you want to kill him before he gets the chance to act. That'd be a good time to do it. After that you're spent and need to rely on your allies, but that's what allies are for, and if you weren't there to kill that Raksha in one chop who knows what could have happened.<br /> <br /> On the other hand if you're facing a pair of Blood Apes with your circle and don't really feel the need to blow out your entire mote pool and half your willpower killing one of them, then don't. Remember, the lesson of Hesiesh is knowing when and how to restrain yourself. In that case just forgo Flash Fire, or use it raw without enhancing both rolls if you just want consistency, and fight using Searing Edge Attacks and/or Essence Igniting Nerve Strikes if you think they're going to be crashed. With Fire Dragon Form up you can save 2m per attack and have about the same odds of hitting after all.<br /> <br /> Then if you want you can Perfect Blazing Blow, or Fiery Blade Attack them to finish them off, or even just regular decisive them. Or be a total dick and hit a spirit with a God-Immolating Strike and a Fiery Blade Attack and set them on double-fire. There's tons of options that aren't turn 1 decisive alpha strikes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Except Fire Dragon does not support at all fighting normally. Searing Edge will only take 2 initiative away from an opponent, without giving it to you, IF your attack hits. Compare to Earth Dragon consistently augmenting damage with Force of The Mountain AND forcing enemies prone AND also augmenting decisive damage, all in the same Charm, worth the same motes as Searing Edge. Or Water Dragon, consistently augmenting decisive damage and increasing wound penalties so that their Form and other Charms become even better over time, for one more mote. All of them workhorses, none require Willpower unlike Perfect Blazing Blow, all of them way better than what Fire Dragon has to offer. Hell, Eye of the Wood Dragon consistently deals more damage than what Searing Edge tries to take away, AND it ignores some soak. Defensively, Earth Dragon offers immense soak and Hardness benefits and Water Dragon has the best defensive DB Charms, while a reroll 1s on attack rolls is all it takes to shut down Flame Flicker. Wound and Mobility penalties are much harder to ignore than onslaught penalties (which everything and its mother ignore), and guess which one Fire uses and which one Water and Earth do? All in all, Fire is not meant to be as strong in a fight as Earth and Water, and it messes with me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T13:25:21-07:00","id":1309273,"title":"","content":"The thing I've been doing for my games is a slightly less powerful version of omni-aura.<br /> <br /> 1. Everyone is assumed to be in every aura at all times<br /> 2. Anything that expends Aura takes you out of Aura until the beginning of your next turn. <br /> <br /> This makes the workhorse Charms more powerful but doesn't let you combo a ton of Aura expending Charms together all at once, and makes Aura expenditure still significant because it weakens you across the spectrum of Aura Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/837-myckou","name":"Myckou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar837_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T14:10:42-07:00","id":1309282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Myckou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1309273#post1309273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing I've been doing for my games is a slightly less powerful version of omni-aura.<br /> <br /> 1. Everyone is assumed to be in every aura at all times<br /> 2. Anything that expends Aura takes you out of Aura until the beginning of your next turn.<br /> <br /> This makes the workhorse Charms more powerful but doesn't let you combo a ton of Aura expending Charms together all at once, and makes Aura expenditure still significant because it weakens you across the spectrum of Aura Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>This wouldn't be so bad if Aura duration charms weren't so expensive. Honestly, trying to combine multiple aura duration charms is a good way to just hemorrhage willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T14:14:08-07:00","id":1309283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1309282#post1309282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This wouldn't be so bad if Aura duration charms weren't so expensive. Honestly, trying to combine multiple aura duration charms is a good way to just hemorrhage willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> *Multiple DB Charms overall, considering about 60% of their Charms have WP costs. Including stuff like Crimson Fang Bite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T14:20:02-07:00","id":1309287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1309283#post1309283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> *Multiple DB Charms overall, considering about 60% of their Charms have WP costs. Including stuff like Crimson Fang Bite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but I don't know any aura charm that doesn't have a willpower cost. It's kind of obnoxious because it means that your major charms have quite a lot of limitations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T15:50:16-07:00","id":1309306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1309263#post1309263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except Fire Dragon does not support at all fighting normally. Searing Edge will only take 2 initiative away from an opponent, without giving it to you, IF your attack hits. Compare to Earth Dragon consistently augmenting damage with Force of The Mountain AND forcing enemies prone AND also augmenting decisive damage, all in the same Charm, worth the same motes as Searing Edge. Or Water Dragon, consistently augmenting decisive damage and increasing wound penalties so that their Form and other Charms become even better over time, for one more mote. All of them workhorses, none require Willpower unlike Perfect Blazing Blow, all of them way better than what Fire Dragon has to offer. Hell, Eye of the Wood Dragon consistently deals more damage than what Searing Edge tries to take away, AND it ignores some soak. Defensively, Earth Dragon offers immense soak and Hardness benefits and Water Dragon has the best defensive DB Charms, while a reroll 1s on attack rolls is all it takes to shut down Flame Flicker. Wound and Mobility penalties are much harder to ignore than onslaught penalties (which everything and its mother ignore), and guess which one Fire uses and which one Water and Earth do? All in all, Fire is not meant to be as strong in a fight as Earth and Water, and it messes with me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so, first of all, nothing rerolls 1s. Fakharu, Octavian, Sigereth, Alhat, Mara, Alveua, Nephwracks, nothing. DBs don't even reroll 1s, only Celestial Exalted do. Unless you're playing a game of &quot;Wyld Hunt's Greatest Hits.&quot; where you skip the entire Hunt and jump right to the ending final battle with anathema each time, you're not facing things that reroll 1s or ignore onslaught penalties. Ignoring onslaught penalties are much the same, except for Fair Folk Cataphracts and creatures with Legendary Size nothing ignores onslauaght penalties. Again, not Octavian, not Alhat, nobody. If every enemy you're facing in your games is rerolling 1s and ignoring onslaught, then your ST is being kind of a dick. Or maybe you like the challenge which would make him less of a dick, I dunno, but it's not what the rules say is normal. What kinds of enemies are you usually fighting?<br /> <br /> Wound penalties aren't perfect either. Tyrant Lizards ignore them to their defense, Vaktri can add them to their damage, and bears and hellboars actually convert them into bonus dice instead.<br /> <br /> <br /> Secondly, yeah, of course the other styles have some charms that are better than charms in Fire Style, it goes both ways. None of the other styles have a defensive charm that you can activate post attack roll. That effect alone is really helpful stretching out motes in prolonged fights. It means you're not going to be spending a ton of motes on an attack that's going to roll amazing and hit you anyway, and not waste motes boosting your defense on attacks that roll badly and whiff you completely.<br /> <br /> Or Fiery Blade Attack, which is great for prolonged fights. Especially since you can't even take a misc action to put out the fire, once it's on you, you're burning until you die or disengage. If you slap that on an enemy early on they're stuck burning until they die, or disengage. Disengaging will be hard because it's an opposed roll against every enemy present in the melee, but then again taking 4L every turn is bad, especially once the wound penalties start racking up and rolling 5 on that (Stamina + Resistance) roll keeps getting harder.<br /> <br /> I don't even think Fire is as good as the other styles in protracted fights, but it's not only good for the alpha strike either.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also Searing Edge is not that bad. Force of the Mountain only adds 2 dice, not 2 levels, of damage, and only adds them pre-soak, so unless it's helping you push your damage past their soak by more than your overwhelming value, it doesn't even do anything. Once you get into Earth Aura it's better, but Searing Edge can trigger on your first attack, which is when you'll be more likely to be withering anyway. Thankfully, the two work well with their respective styles. Fire can only use light weapons, so with their high accuracy and low damage post-soak damage is good. Earth on the other hand is stuck with a crappy heavy weapon, but Force of the Mountain can help mitigate that by dealing a bunch of extra damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T15:56:53-07:00","id":1309310,"title":"","content":"I'm not normally one to call people out but at this point this should just get it's own topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T16:14:11-07:00","id":1309315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1309306#post1309306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, so, first of all, nothing rerolls 1s. Fakharu, Octavian, Sigereth, Alhat, Mara, Alveua, Nephwracks, nothing. DBs don't even reroll 1s, only Celestial Exalted do. Unless you're playing a game of &quot;Wyld Hunt's Greatest Hits.&quot; where you skip the entire Hunt and jump right to the ending final battle with anathema each time, you're not facing things that reroll 1s or ignore onslaught penalties. Ignoring onslaught penalties are much the same, except for Fair Folk Cataphracts and creatures with Legendary Size nothing ignores onslauaght penalties. Again, not Octavian, not Alhat, nobody. If every enemy you're facing in your games is rerolling 1s and ignoring onslaught, then your ST is being kind of a dick. Or maybe you like the challenge which would make him less of a dick, I dunno, but it's not what the rules say is normal. What kinds of enemies are you usually fighting?<br /> <br /> Wound penalties aren't perfect either. Tyrant Lizards ignore them to their defense, Vaktri can add them to their damage, and bears and hellboars actually convert them into bonus dice instead.<br /> <br /> <br /> Secondly, yeah, of course the other styles have some charms that are better than charms in Fire Style, it goes both ways. None of the other styles have a defensive charm that you can activate post attack roll. That effect alone is really helpful stretching out motes in prolonged fights. It means you're not going to be spending a ton of motes on an attack that's going to roll amazing and hit you anyway, and not waste motes boosting your defense on attacks that roll badly and whiff you completely.<br /> <br /> Or Fiery Blade Attack, which is great for prolonged fights. Especially since you can't even take a misc action to put out the fire, once it's on you, you're burning until you die or disengage. If you slap that on an enemy early on they're stuck burning until they die, or disengage. Disengaging will be hard because it's an opposed roll against every enemy present in the melee, but then again taking 4L every turn is bad, especially once the wound penalties start racking up and rolling 5 on that (Stamina + Resistance) roll keeps getting harder.<br /> <br /> I don't even think Fire is as good as the other styles in protracted fights, but it's not only good for the alpha strike either.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also Searing Edge is not that bad. Force of the Mountain only adds 2 dice, not 2 levels, of damage, and only adds them pre-soak, so unless it's helping you push your damage past their soak by more than your overwhelming value, it doesn't even do anything. Once you get into Earth Aura it's better, but Searing Edge can trigger on your first attack, which is when you'll be more likely to be withering anyway. Thankfully, the two work well with their respective styles. Fire can only use light weapons, so with their high accuracy and low damage post-soak damage is good. Earth on the other hand is stuck with a crappy heavy weapon, but Force of the Mountain can help mitigate that by dealing a bunch of extra damage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Melee Supernal, Lunar Witch, BGs with Might, and other DBs. That's what I've been fighting so far. Not that I have used FD extensively on any situation except against other DBs, but even then Fire + Snake loses to even Melee.<br /> <br /> Ok, to break it down. Even without reroll 1s, Flame Flicker can be useless when an opponent doesn't roll 1s or rolls not-enough-to-raise-your-Defense-to-parry-their-attack 1s. It is not reliable, it is not at all the best defensive option in IMA or even close, and even at max efficiency it's only a post-roll half-free excellency (If you're in Fire Aura). Let alone that it works off of Parry only, instead of Evasion which at least could benefit from Dodge Charms to enhance the benefits, or even from Martial Arts that combo with Fire Dragon such as Snake Style. <br /> <br /> Searing Edge is stupid bad if you compare it to every single other workhorse. Sure, you gained 6i and your opponent lost 7 instead of 5. Great deal. Compare to Force of the Mountain, which under Aura (SEA has no Aura benefit btw) deals 2.5 initiative damage on average WHICH DOES ADD TO YOUR OWN INITIATIVE, unlike SEA. Also it prones people due to the Smashing tag, riddling them with penalties and potentially becoming a You Are Already Dead situation if your Dodge isn't up to par. Also it benefits Decisive damage with double 10s, an incredibly good benefit for 3m. SEA IS bad and contributes to the whole &quot;Fire Dragon wastes initiative from every pore and never recovers it&quot; issue with FD. Eye of the Wood Dragon deals more damage, does recover that initiative it deals AND it ignores soak so you can't even say &quot;but me post-soak&quot;. SEA is worse than any other offensive option in IMA except for Air Dragon which just straight up does not have initiative regain.<br /> <br /> &quot;Wound penalty is ignored by The Apex Predator Of Legend, a single Elemental type can mess with it, and a couple animals ignore it to attack and turn it into attack dice&quot; is not going to put a single dent in how good Water is in comparison to Fire, mate.<br /> <br /> Also, consider that in order to combo this with anything that's not the hilariously dumb mess that is Steel Devil? You need to go unarmed. No twin blade Artifacts for you, no +5 non-Charm attack bonus, no Overwhelming goodness, no huge damage bonuses.<br /> <br /> Fiery Blade Attack is pointless when you don't have that 4i to pay for the attack, or when paying it will mean a stiff breeze crashes you to oblivion. Even when it goes off, an opponent can just disengage from you, making your expenditure pointless without giving you ways to regain that lost initiative. Also, it's Essence 3.<br /> <br /> In short words, Fire IS horrible at anything that's not alpha strikes or &quot;Enter the fight with your best Join Battle, try your damnedest to crash one or two people, launch Perfect Blazing Blow, be useless the rest of the fight again&quot; because it doesn't have ways to recover initiative, wastes too many motes, doesn't combo with anything unless you go unarmed (Steel Devil isn't valid and Violet Bier hasn't come out yet), and literally every other style except Air does better than it does at normal fights.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T04:35:39-07:00","id":1309399,"title":"","content":"My idea was that the DB, when he use a charm that it's not the of the same element, can choose to mantain is Aura or he can <b>change</b> the element of the Aura at the end of his turn, but in any case, he never lose his Aura.<br /> <br /> It's a less powerful version of &quot;you're in every elemental Aura ever&quot;, basically treating every charm as balanced unless you want to change your Aura element.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you just buy the power of count your Aura like it's alway in a particular element (with the Caste one being the default). You do this using some kind of merit (like, several different Merits or one big merit).<br /> <br /> Or a combination of both.<br /> <br /> What do you think? It's a little more complex than giving flat out omni-Aura to every DB but I think's it's more interesting from a in-universe point of view so not every DB is a master of every element.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25288-shapechanger","name":"Shapechanger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25288_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T04:39:27-07:00","id":1309401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shapechanger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1309399#post1309399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My idea was that the DB, when he use a charm that it's not the of the same element, can choose to mantain is Aura or he can <b>change</b> the element of the Aura at the end of his turn, but in any case, he never lose his Aura.<br /> <br /> It's a less powerful version of &quot;you're in every elemental Aura ever&quot;, basically treating every charm as balanced unless you want to change your Aura element.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you just buy the power of count your Aura like it's alway in a particular element (with the Caste one being the default). You do this using some kind of merit (like, several different Merits or one big merit).<br /> <br /> Or a combination of both.<br /> <br /> What do you think? It's a little more complex than giving flat out omni-Aura to every DB but I think's it's more interesting from a in-universe point of view so not every DB is a master of every element.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't actually help Dragon blooded all it does is means they still get screwed out of aura long effects which should be scenelong but aren't because of a poorly thought out keyword.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T04:44:25-07:00","id":1309403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1309401#post1309401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't actually help Dragon blooded all it does is means they still get screwed out of aura long effects which should be scenelong but aren't because of a poorly thought out keyword.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if they use a Charm that consume Aura.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25288-shapechanger","name":"Shapechanger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25288_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T04:46:16-07:00","id":1309404,"title":"","content":"I don't think &quot;poorly thought out&quot; is the right term. Aura duration does exactly what the devs intended. You just don't like it. Because... it makes dragon blooded weaker? Like it's supposed to do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T04:48:02-07:00","id":1309405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shapechanger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1309403#post1309403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only if they use a Charm that consume Aura.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not if you change it to another element. Personally, looking at the homebrew a clutch of dragons a system where you can buy any charm but it costs more out of aspect but you can always use it and combine it with other charms looks a lot more fun and balanced than something like aura thay cuts down your charmset to 1/5 of what you can use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T04:52:52-07:00","id":1309406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1309405#post1309405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not if you change it to another element. Personally, looking at the homebrew a clutch of dragons a system where you can buy any charm but it costs more out of aspect but you can always use it and combine it with other charms looks a lot more fun and balanced than something like aura thay cuts down your charmset to 1/5 of what you can use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmmm. I must have understood wrong the Aura-based Charm mechanic, because I was under the impression that interrupting Aura happened the moment when you activated a charm that was not Balanced and could only be restarted at the end of the turn. And the Scene-long Charm that required Aura finish when you drop out of Aura.<br /> <br /> If that's the case, wouldn't the first Option prevent that in any case since you can just choose to not change your Aura but mantain the previous one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25288-shapechanger","name":"Shapechanger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25288_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T04:56:40-07:00","id":1309408,"title":"","content":"Plus, aura only cuts your charmset down to 1/5 if you have an equal number of charms of each element. <br /> <br /> Pro tip: Don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T05:01:36-07:00","id":1309410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1309408#post1309408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, aura only cuts your charmset down to 1/5 if you have an equal number of charms of each element. <br /> <br /> Pro tip: Don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>No in most cases one element gets everything and you only have two charms you can use. So without homebrew charms or evocations you have almost nothing or exactly nothing until signature aura. You cannot look at the uneven combat distribution and tell me aura was a fully test mechanic. There are some elements that get way better abilities than other ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T05:03:50-07:00","id":1309411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shapechanger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1309406#post1309406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mmmm. I must have understood wrong the Aura-based Charm mechanic, because I was under the impression that interrupting Aura happened the moment when you activated a charm that was not Balanced and could only be restarted at the end of the turn. And the Scene-long Charm that required Aura finish when you drop out of Aura.<br /> <br /> If that's the case, wouldn't the first Option prevent that in any case since you can just choose to not change your Aura but mantain the previous one?</div> </div> </div> </div>You cannot if you hit bonfire. If you treat everything as balance it's slightly better but there are still some fundimental issues with some charms that really only work with aura.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T05:08:04-07:00","id":1309413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1309411#post1309411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You cannot if you hit bonfire. If you treat everything as balance it's slightly better but there are still some fundimental issues with some charms that really only work with aura.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's more or less the intent of the first option. Every Charm is Balanced unless you choose to switch your Aura to a different Element (maybe because you just activated an Aura-Charm that give a juicy bonus if you are in a particular Aura and you want that). But even then, you switch the element, but the Aura don't stop.<br /> <br /> In the second option you buy a Merit so every charm of a certain element to be Balanced.<br /> <br /> In both cases you jusy keep Aura going since, for my understanding, what cause problems is the Aura stop working, not the fact that the Aura is of a particular element.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25288-shapechanger","name":"Shapechanger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25288_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T05:16:26-07:00","id":1309414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shapechanger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1309413#post1309413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's more or less the intent of the first option. Every Charm is Balanced unless you choose to switch your Aura to a different Element (maybe because you just activated an Aura-Charm that give a juicy bonus if you are in a particular Aura and you want that). But even then, you switch the element, but the Aura don't stop.<br /> <br /> In the second option you buy a Merit so every charm of a certain element to be Balanced.<br /> <br /> In both cases you jusy keep Aura going since, for my understanding, what cause problems is the Aura stop working, not the fact that the Aura is of a particular element.</div> </div> </div> </div>It matters due to how many effects are tied to specific aura.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T09:02:06-07:00","id":1309459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shapechanger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1309413#post1309413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's more or less the intent of the first option. Every Charm is Balanced unless you choose to switch your Aura to a different Element (maybe because you just activated an Aura-Charm that give a juicy bonus if you are in a particular Aura and you want that). But even then, you switch the element, but the Aura don't stop.<br /> <br /> In the second option you buy a Merit so every charm of a certain element to be Balanced.<br /> <br /> In both cases you jusy keep Aura going since, for my understanding, what cause problems is the Aura stop working, not the fact that the Aura is of a particular element.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you may be misunderstanding the aura mechanic.<br /> <br /> Under the heading &quot;The Aura affects Charms in multiple ways&quot;, there's the bullet point that reads &quot;Some Aura Charms have &quot;Duration: Aura,&quot; indicating that they last only as long as the Dragon-Blood remains in <b>that element's</b> Aura.&quot; Bolding mine.<br /> <br /> So if you swap your aura over to a different element, all your duration: Aura charms would drop as well. Now, unlike Epimetheus, I don't think this is a bad thing. This is part of the core balance of the entire DB splat. It's about the only way that the DB don't just rofl-stomp everything in the setting. Plus it drives individual DB to specialize into individual elements. <br /> <br /> I think it adds flavour and balance but at the same time I can see why some people really hate the overall amount of bookeeping and how it locks away a lot of your stuff. That's why i suggested upthread to basically treat all charms as balanced so long as they aren't aura charms themselves, and to also get rid of aura lock from bonfire anima. I think it's silly that a fire aspect basically can't spec into water aura stuff if they want to because they'll basically always lose their core charms if they're in a fight that's strenuous enough that they're spending lots of essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T09:19:20-07:00","id":1309462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1309459#post1309459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Under the heading &quot;The Aura affects Charms in multiple ways&quot;, there's the bullet point that reads &quot;Some Aura Charms have &quot;Duration: Aura,&quot; indicating that they last only as long as the Dragon-Blood remains in <b>that element's</b> Aura.&quot; Bolding mine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I missed that one. Yeah, it limit a little the first option I proposed.<br /> <br /> Speaking of the limitation of Aura, I don't think it's necessarly a bad thing either, but I prefer to add mechanics then remove them. So, I'll prefer for the DB to have the ability to off-set the problem instead of just giving a blank all-element Aura mechanics. In that way, sure, powerful DB like Her Redness and PG's can basically combo every charm and steamroll everythiing that's not a equally powerful Celestial Exalted, but 'down to Earth' DB are still limited and so the power-balance of the world is more or less kept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25288-shapechanger","name":"Shapechanger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25288_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T14:51:55-07:00","id":1309515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1309459#post1309459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you may be misunderstanding the aura mechanic.<br /> <br /> Under the heading &quot;The Aura affects Charms in multiple ways&quot;, there's the bullet point that reads &quot;Some Aura Charms have &quot;Duration: Aura,&quot; indicating that they last only as long as the Dragon-Blood remains in <b>that element's</b> Aura.&quot; Bolding mine.<br /> <br /> So if you swap your aura over to a different element, all your duration: Aura charms would drop as well. Now, unlike Epimetheus, I don't think this is a bad thing. This is part of the core balance of the entire DB splat. It's about the only way that the DB don't just rofl-stomp everything in the setting. Plus it drives individual DB to specialize into individual elements. <br /> <br /> I think it adds flavour and balance but at the same time I can see why some people really hate the overall amount of bookeeping and how it locks away a lot of your stuff. That's why i suggested upthread to basically treat all charms as balanced so long as they aren't aura charms themselves, and to also get rid of aura lock from bonfire anima. I think it's silly that a fire aspect basically can't spec into water aura stuff if they want to because they'll basically always lose their core charms if they're in a fight that's strenuous enough that they're spending lots of essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because aura duration charms are expensive. And are only useful if they have multiple turns of use. A system where the charm is still on but suppressed till you get aura back would be more fair for the commitment you need. <br /> <br /> Again these charms are already levels below what celestials get and I would prefer they be even weaker if that's the intent then this unfun. Because losing access to charms, buying dead charms, having systems where you lose out on powers to use. These are not hallmarks of a fun system.<br /> <br /> This is why this thread started because someone wants to use dragon blooded by his players don't want to use the aura system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 05-02-2019, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T14:56:02-07:00","id":1309516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1308634-ignoring-aura-options?p=1309515#post1309515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because aura duration charms are expensive. And are only useful if they have multiple turns of use. A system where the charm is still on but suppressed till you get aura back would be more fair for the commitment you need.<br /> <br /> Again these charms are already levels below what celestials get and I would prefer they be even weaker if that's the intent then this unfun. Because losing access to charms, buying dead charms, having systems where you lose out on powers to use. These are not hallmarks of a fun system.<br /> <br /> This is why this thread started because someone wants to use dragon blooded by his players don't want to use the aura system.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm gonna second this &quot;Suppressed until you go back to Aura but still active&quot; idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}